  "details": "Steps to reproduce:\n\n1. Have an InputUse event that prints the value of the first argument (the pressed/unpressed bool)\n\n2. Press & hold trigger/mouse to start an InputUse, and \"true\" will be printed, as expected\n\n3. While still holding the trigger/mouse, open the menu (open full menu in VR, not just quick menu. In Desktop, just press escape)\n\n4. Let go of the trigger/mouse. No \"false\" event is printed\n\n5. Exit menu, \"false\" still isn't printed. Only after clicking again will it print \"true\" then \"false\".\n\nNot having the false/unpressed event happen if the menu is open means the button can get stuck pressed down, which can cause trouble if part of the world interaction involves holding down the button.\n\nThis issue applies at least to InputUse and InputJump.\n\nIt does not apply to InputMove* in Desktop because the menu can't be opened while pressing a move key in Desktop. But it might apply in VR, I haven't checked.\n\nSuggested solutions:\n\n1. If the button is being pressed when the menu is open, allow the unpressed event to be sent *once* while the menu is closed.\n\n2. If the button is being pressed when the menu is open, immediately send the unpressed event. Care should be taken to not send it again once the menu is closed, if the player continues to hold down the button.\n\n3. Same as 2, except as soon as the menu is closed, if the button is still held down, send the pressed event again.",
